      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing-mark reader (reuse verbatim)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs">
        `Read(byte[])` (`:68`) returns `DocxAnnotationReadResult { Comments, Revisions }`; `RecoveredRevision` (`:327-348`) carries kind/id/author/date/text/anchorText/paragraphHint. Call it on the load-time bytes; do not touch the reader.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Load orchestration seam" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs">
        `LoadAsync` (`:168`) — extend to run the reader alongside the mammoth convert and add the recovered-revisions list to the Load response (additive, mirror-first).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Declare rigor (FULL). Confirm deps 010 (paraId map on Load), 012 (paraId anchoring), 022 (E1 cutover) are ✅. Load bff-extensions.md + the ADRs. Read design §7 + §2 and the reader source — confirm `Read` reads all-authorship revisions and do NOT plan any reader change.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Design the additive Load-response projection">Add an additive `importedRevisions` (or equivalent) field to the Load-response contract, mirror-first (`compose-contracts.ts` ↔ server DTO). Each item carries the `RecoveredRevision` fields + the E2 `paraId` for the anchoring paragraph. snake_case on the wire; do not invent a parallel schema — reuse the `RecoveredRevision` shape.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Wire the reader into LoadAsync">In `LoadAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:168`), run `DocxAnnotationReader.Read` on the load-time `.docx` bytes alongside the mammoth convert; map each `RecoveredRevision` onto the response, attaching the `paraId` from the E2 pre-parse map (task 010). Empty list (not null) when the doc has no revisions.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Render imported revisions in the editor mount">In `ComposeEditor.tsx`, on mount, render each imported revision as a first-class R2 `insertion`/`deletion` mark (author/date attributed, accept/reject-able) anchored by `paraId` — instead of the mammoth-flattened prose. Do NOT add any TipTap Pro/TrackChanges module; use the existing home-grown marks.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Anchor + fuzzy fallback">Anchor imported revisions by `paraId` first; retain the `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy fallback (textPattern + Levenshtein + paragraphHint) for the cross-Word-session case where paraIds were regenerated externally.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Unit tests">Add Load-projection unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`: a Word-redlined fixture yields the recovered revisions on the Load response with correct kind/author/date + paraId; a no-revision fixture yields an empty list, not null. Mock at the SPE facade boundary (ADR-038; no transport mocks).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify + report">Build BFF + shared lib; run the new tests; run the NetArchTest facade check; report publish-size delta (~0 expected) + CVE; state the Placement Justification; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (LoadAsync projects RecoveredRevision)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts (additive imported-revisions field)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (imported revisions rendered as first-class marks)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ (Load-projection tests)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline; CVE scan; NetArchTest facade result; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A `.docx` redlined in Word (existing `w:ins`/`w:del`, any authorship) opens in Compose with those revisions rendered as first-class tracked changes — visible and accept/reject-able — NOT flattened to prose (FR-24 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`LoadAsync` runs the EXISTING `DocxAnnotationReader.Read` verbatim (reader unmodified) and projects `RecoveredRevision` (kind/author/date/text + paraId) onto the Load response; a no-revision doc yields an empty list, not null.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Imported revisions anchor primarily by `w14:paraId` (E2); the `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy match is retained as the cross-Word-session fallback.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rendering uses the R2 home-grown `insertion`/`deletion` marks on the MIT TipTap base — no `@tiptap-pro/*` and no TipTap TrackChanges module added (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type appears in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size reported absolute + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline (≈0 expected; no new NuGet); no new HIGH CVE; Placement Justification stated citing bff-extensions.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Load-projection unit tests exist at the KEEP path and pass; BFF + shared-lib builds green (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI/ctor-null tests — ADR-038).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

